title: '[eth-rpc]: add resumable block sync and improve CLI arguments'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |
    ### Resumable block sync
    - New block_sync module syncs backward from the latest finalized block to the first EVM block, with crash-safe checkpoint tracking via a sync_state SQLite table.
    - On restart, fills only the top gap (new blocks) and bottom gap (remaining backfill) without re-syncing completed ranges.
    - Auto-discovers and persists `first_evm_block` — the lowest block with EVM support on the chain.
    - Chain identity verification: Store genesis hash in sync_state and validate on startup; detect stale boundaries after reorgs.

    ### CLI rework (breaking)
    - Replace `--database-url` with `--base-path` (database file is auto-named `eth-rpc.db`)
    - Replace `--index-last-n-blocks` with `--sync` (syncs all finalized blocks down to the first EVM block)
    - Replace `--cache-size` with `--prune` (in-memory DB, keeps latest N blocks)
    - Remove `--earliest-receipt-block` (replaced by auto-discovered `first_evm_block`)
crates:
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: minor
